What libtpms needs to build on Windows against MSVC's runtime, as the
MSVC QEMU's TPM (track M20; scripts/build-deps.sh compiles it with
clang-cl). Headers in src/win32, none used by libtpms's own
build: compat.h, force-included, gives the POSIX code paths
clock_gettime() for CLOCK_REALTIME (timespec_get) and CLOCK_MONOTONIC
(the UCRT's clock()), and asprintf, dprintf, strndup and index;
unistd.h is the C runtime's io.h and process.h;
config.h is configure's two defines for TPM 2.0 on OpenSSL;
netinet/in.h and endian.h are byte order conversions;
regex.h is PCRE2's POSIX wrapper. And three Windows branches in the
TPM 2.0 headers: little-endian, 64-bit Windows' OpenSSL word size
(SIXTY_FOUR_BIT), and the simulator's headers without sockets.

